{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":136895,"duration_api_ms":178576,"num_turns":12,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"2445bb6f-8fe1-4ea0-a027-9dabbcbc8988","total_cost_usd":0.63207235,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35291,"cache_read_input_tokens":210500,"output_tokens":6671,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":35291,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":131,"outputTokens":6328,"cacheReadInputTokens":281051,"cacheCreationInputTokens":63654,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.13944360000000003,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":7,"outputTokens":6671,"cacheReadInputTokens":210500,"cacheCreationInputTokens":35291,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.49262874999999995,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All five amendments identify real, verified issues. Four are carbonate-solver consistency or data correctness defects, and one is a pre-existing test failure blocking cargo test. I verified each claim against the source code: redundant bicarbonate mutations (confirmed at water_change.rs:67,85), the pH 7.0 fallback masking acid crashes (confirmed at chemistry.rs:82-88), the failing shrimp test (confirmed exists), the pH clamp/solve inconsistency (confirmed though line numbers in invariants.rs are off — actual clamp is at line 10 not 89-95), and the preset pH miscalculation (manually verified soft_acidic yields ~pH 9.2, moderate ~8.3, hard_shrimp ~8.7).","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-f4b7f286","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified. water_change.rs:67 and :85 independently mutate bicarbonate_mg_total, which is then overwritten at :95 by resolve_carbonate_state. The carbonate_state_contract.md (line 123) explicitly prohibits independent mutation of this cached projection. The mutations are dead writes today but create a maintenance hazard if resolve ordering changes. The rescale_totals_for_volume case (water.rs:204) is numerically benign but conceptually wrong for the same reason."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-3a75c43a","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified. chemistry.rs:82-88 returns pH 7.0 when alkalinity <= 1e-9 with nonzero DIC, and nitrogen_cycle.rs clamps alkalinity to 0.0 via .max(0.0). This combination means nitrification-driven alkalinity depletion — the textbook acid crash scenario — is silently reported as neutral pH. For a tank simulation where acid crashes are a primary gameplay hazard, this is a significant correctness gap. At minimum a structured warning event should fire when this fallback triggers with nonzero DIC."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-02f18c66","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified. The test exists at shrimp_population.rs:102-138, and shrimp.rs is modified (visible in git status). A perpetually failing test makes cargo test red, which masks new regressions from the carbonate solver work. This must be resolved — either by fixing the population dynamics or updating expectations — before merging."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-ae57349f","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified with a line-number correction: the pH clamp is at invariants.rs:10 (not lines 89-95 as stated), but the defect is real. resolve_carbonate_state writes raw solver pH (chemistry.rs ~line 169), enforce_invariants clamps water.ph to 5.5..=8.5, snapshot.rs:76-81 recomputes carbonate_eq from unclamped DIC/alkalinity while using the clamped pH for NH3 (line 87-88), and save.rs:344 re-solves from unclamped inputs undoing the clamp. Any state with solver pH outside 5.5-8.5 has inconsistent chemistry and non-idempotent save-loads. The fix — clamping at the solver boundary or reprojecting all derived fields together — is sound."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-22793191","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified by manual calculation through the solver's quadratic. soft_acidic.toml (DIC=12.0 mg C/L, Alk=1.07 meq/L) yields ~pH 9.2, moderate.toml (15.0/1.249) yields ~pH 8.3, hard_shrimp.toml (21.0/1.785) yields ~pH 8.7. A preset labeled 'soft_acidic' producing pH 9.2 is plainly wrong, and two presets hit the 8.5 invariant ceiling immediately. These presets were tuned for the old shortcut and are now materially broken. validate() only checks non-negativity, providing no guard. Either recalibrate the DIC/alk pairs or add derived-pH validation."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"12c14d2f-ed62-4213-87cc-4ec1d00463cd"}
